GATE CSE 1991 [PDS]:
Consider the following pseudo-code (all data items are of type integer):

```pascal
procedure P(a, b, c);
  a := 2;
  c := a + b;
end {P};
begin
  x := 1;
  y := 5;
  z := 100;
  P(x, x*y, z);
  write ('x = ', x, 'z = ', z)
end;
```

Determine its output, if the parameters are passed to the procedure P by (i) value, (ii) reference and (iii) name.

GATE CSE 1991 [PDS]:
For the following pseudo-code, indicate the output if (i) static scope rules and (ii) dynamic scope rules are used.

```pascal
var a, b : integer;
procedure P;
  a := 5; b := 10
end {P};
procedure Q;
  var a, b : integer;
  P;
end {Q};
begin
  a := 1; b := 2;
  Q;
